WEBVTT

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.200
and we start to blur the distinction
between what is fact and what is story.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:32.896
On the fifth rung,

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.640
we develop conclusions
based on our assumptions.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.480
This is also where
our emotional reactions are created.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.576
On the sixth rung,

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.496
we adjust our beliefs
about the world around us,

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.416
including the person or people involved

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.456
in our experience of the moment.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.096
On the seventh and final rung,

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.977
we take action
based on our adjusted beliefs.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.136
Still with me? Great!

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.936
Let's take a real-life example

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.840
and run it up the ladder
to see how this all works.